        "notes": "Rims of the 9,224 craters in the PH9224GT catalogue, each drawn as a circle of its published centre and radius on a 24 m grid. An automated detector found them in topography and images, and candidates were checked by hand. The four largest entries, 8.6 to 17.9 km across, are wider than Stickney and carry no IAU name; they are shown as published. Unmarked ground is the Monochrome mosaic in gray at 35% brightness and 6 bits per channel, a presentation choice: the rim color differs by at least 40 OKLab units from every dimmed gray. The color is the Trek layer’s symbol for its smallest class."
